<title>BRAZIL: Banco Real first half net lower.</title>
<headline>Banco Real first half net lower.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian private bank Banco Real on Monday issued the following 1997 first half consolidated results.</p>
<p>		     1997		   1996</p>
<p>    Net	    110 million		236 million</p>
<p>    Net worth    1.688 bln	    N/A</p>
<p>    Total assets 18.16 bln	    N/A</p>
<p>NOTE: All figures in Brazilian reais.</p>
<p>The bank said its first half earnings last year included 191 million reais in revenues stemming from the sale of so-called FCVS debt paper.</p>
<p>It said it showed an annualized return on equity of 13.5 percent in the 1997 first half.</p>
<p>((--Fatima Cristina, Sao Paulo Newsroom 5511 2485412))</p>
</text>
